{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"fbf89bbe1a09dcfb","name":"card_event_spearhead","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_spearhead","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SPEARHEAD","text":"Destroy a friendly unit and adjacent units. Your units get +X+X, where X is units destroyed.","flavorText":"In a military context, the term \"spearhead\" refers to a unit or force that leads an attack or an offensive operation. It is a metaphorical reference to the pointed head of a spear, which is used to penetrate and break through enemy defenses. The spearhead unit is typically composed of highly skilled and well-equipped troops, often armored or mechanized, and is tasked with the initial assault to achieve a breakthrough in the enemy's front lines. Operation Bagration and the Battle of Kursk were two significant WWII offensives conducted by the Red Army, both involving spearhead operations. The Battle of Kursk, which took place in July and August 1943, witnessed the Red Army launching a counteroffensive against German forces. Spearhead divisions, strategically concentrated and equipped with tanks and heavy artillery, led the assault, breaking through German lines and setting the stage for subsequent Soviet victories. Operation Bagration, launched in June 1944, was a massive Soviet offensive on the Eastern Front aimed at destroying German Army Group Center. Spearhead units comprising armored and mechanized divisions, supported by infantry and artillery, spearheaded the attack, rapidly advancing deep into enemy territory and encircling German forces.","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_spearhead","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_spearhead_title","SourceString":"SPEARHEAD","LocalizedString":"SPEARHEAD"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":2,"Text":{"Na